invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_word.h
catches: p256_equiv_test_sum
reason: the 128-bit sum, the form of the add with carry that gcc compiles
  for a machine other than x86-64, adds its two words and leaves the
  carry in out, so every chain of words drops the carries between them.
  No compiler check runs on picks this form, so bin/p256_equiv_test
  never compiles the line: bin/p256_equiv_test_sum names the form and
  holds every sum on it to p256_field.c's and p256_scalar.c's.

--- old
    ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)a + b + *carry;
--- new
    ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)a + b;
